    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0019" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation 3A/521: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-05T21:00:00-03:00">January 5, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. For Duggan from Spaeth. With further reference to our cable 22, 5th,<anchor
                        n="15" xml:id="d5-f1"/> both resolution and summary of replies were approved
                    unanimously although Chilean member<anchor n="16" xml:id="d5-f2"/> initially
                    opposed resolution and sought to delay action, informing me privately that he
                    wanted time to consult his Government. Argentine<anchor n="17" xml:id="d5-f3"/>
                    was absent. [Spaeth.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d5-f1" n="15" xml:id="d5-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f2" n="16" xml:id="d5-f2-content">
                <p>Alfredo Rodriguez MacIver.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f3" n="17" xml:id="d5-f3-content">
                <p>The Argentine member of the Committee was Guillermo de Achával.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
